81. What is a Data Source?
A data source in Terraform is used to read or fetch existing information from a provider, instead of creating a new resource.
data "aws_ami" "amazon_linux_mumbai" {
  provider    = aws.mumbai
  most_recent = true
  owners      = [var.ami_owner]

  filter {
    name   = "name"
    values = [var.ami_filter_name]
  }
}

82. Difference between Resource and Data Source
Resource	Data Source
Creates/manages infrastructure	Reads/fetches existing information
Can create, update, and delete	Normally read-only from Terraform's perspective
Syntax: resource	Syntax: data
Reference: aws_instance.web.id	Reference: data.aws_ami.ubuntu.id


83. When would you use a Data Source?

Use a data source when the information/resource already exists and you need to get its details.

Common examples:

1. Find an existing AMI

data "aws_ami" "ubuntu" {
  most_recent = true
  owners      = ["099720109477"]
}

2. Get an existing VPC

data "aws_vpc" "existing" {
  id = "vpc-123456"
}

3. Get an existing subnet

data "aws_subnet" "existing" {
  id = "subnet-123456"
}

Then use the information in a resource:

resource "aws_instance" "web" {
  ami       = data.aws_ami.ubuntu.id
  subnet_id = data.aws_subnet.existing.id
}
Interview answer
A data source is used to read existing information from a provider. A resource is used to create and manage 
infrastructure, while a data source is used to retrieve information about existing infrastructure. We use data sources
when we need to use something that already exists, such as an existing AMI, VPC, or subnet.


